  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HIV/TB - Western Africa - Multicountry Western Africa ANCS (01-Jan-2017-31-Dec-2019)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multicountry Western Africa ANCS, TB/HIV, Alliance Nationale des Communaut&#xe9;s pour la Sant&#xe9; - S&#xe9;n&#xe9;gal (ANCS)This program has the following goals: To improve HIV/TB/Hepatitis harm reduction services and promote human rights of People Who Inject Drugs in five West African countries (Senegal, Burkina Faso, Cape Verde, Ivory Coast and Guinea Bissau). The objectives of this program are: Objective 1: Improve the availability of strategic information to guide risk-reduction interventions for people who inject drugs in the five countries in West Africa (Burkina Faso, Cape Verde, Ivory Coast, Guinea-Bissau and Senegal).  Objective 2: Build capacity among community actors and people who inject drugs on risk reduction to improve health and human rights services for people who inject drugs.  Objective 3: Improve the social and legal environment to facilitate the implementation of risk-reduction activities among people who inject drugs in West Africa (Burkina Faso, Cape Verde, Ivory Coast, Guinea-Bissau and Senegal).  Objective 4: Implement model harm reduction projects and document best practices to be replicated in West Africa (Burkina Faso, Cape Verde, Ivory Coast, Guinea-Bissau and Senegal)</narrative>
  </description>
